    "evidence_text": "Cow Creek (Montana)\n\n Today, modern highways have by passed Cow Creek, and the buffalo and the nomadic Indian are gone.\n\nLithia Springs Creek\n\n It is approximately 3.2 mi long and flows through Point Township.\n\n The watershed of the creek has an area of 8.96 sqmi .\n\n It has a named tributary known as Johnson Creek.\n\n At least one bridge more than 20 ft long crosses the creek.\n\n The creek is considered to be a Coldwater Fishery and a Migratory Fishery.\n\n It is inhabited by wild trout and possibly a few other species of fish.\n\nLocks Creek\nLocks Creek is a 1.9 mi stream in San Mateo County, California.\n It is the largest tributary of Frenchmans Creek, a larger stream.\n\nEast Branch South Fork Eel River\n\n Major tributaries of the East Branch include Buck Mountain Creek, Squaw Creek, Rays Creek, and Tom Long Creek.\n\n The river flows west, turns north, and flows west again, through rugged terrain in the Coast Range of California.\n\n The East Branch is the South Fork Eel's largest tributary.\n\nRed Rock River (Montana)\n\n Its drainage basin covers over 1548 mi2 .\n\nDarling River\n\n Including its longest contiguous tributaries it is 2844 km long, making it the longest river system in Australia.\n\nFrenchmans Creek (California)\nFrenchmans Creek is a 4.4 mi stream in San Mateo County, California.\n Locks Creek is its largest tributary.\n\nJemez River\n\n The East Fork Jemez River is about 22 mi long.\n\n Both San Antonio Creek and the East Fork Jemez River flow through intricate meanders along their courses.\n\n The East Fork Jemez is a National Wild and Scenic River.\n\nFrenchmans Creek (New South Wales)\n\nTomichi Creek\n\n Congress Creek drains into Tomichi west of Old Monarch Pass where it flows south toward Sargents.\n\n Hot Springs Reservoir drains down Wanita Canyon flowing into Tomichi Creek just west of Doyleville.\n\n At Parlin, Quartz Creek flows from Pitkin and Ohio into Tomichi Creek.\n\n A map can be viewed at the BLM Colorado website here.",
